to do as much as I can.

00:25:21.413 --> 00:25:24.104
But like even following
that plan, I was like,

00:25:24.104 --> 00:25:27.056
"Fuck, he's kind of like, hitting me."

00:25:27.056 --> 00:25:29.305
I know he's getting tired,
I know this is the plan,

00:25:29.305 --> 00:25:31.604
but I'm still scared.

00:25:31.604 --> 00:25:34.025
I was like, I think there was
a moment where I was like,

00:25:34.025 --> 00:25:37.667
"I need to start hitting
him in order to win

00:25:37.667 --> 00:25:38.963
or I will lose."

00:25:38.963 --> 00:25:40.635
- 'Cause obviously the points, right?

00:25:40.635 --> 00:25:41.944
- Yeah, the points.
- If it goes to technical.

00:25:41.944 --> 00:25:42.777
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:25:42.777 --> 00:25:45.000
And I felt like I was losing
like the entire first round,

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:47.293
but I think it went even.

00:25:47.293 --> 00:25:49.418
Yeah, it was complete, like,

00:25:49.418 --> 00:25:50.848
it was crazy seeing it from the outside.

00:25:50.848 --> 00:25:53.072
'Cause it felt weird as fuck.

00:25:53.072 --> 00:25:54.844
- Like how much of what,

00:25:54.844 --> 00:25:56.500
how much do you remember
being in the ring?

00:25:56.500 --> 00:25:58.598
Do you remember like, people
chanting your name, 'cause you.

00:25:58.598 --> 00:25:59.696
- I do remember that.

00:25:59.696 --> 00:26:01.952
And like I was like, "That's nice."

00:26:01.952 --> 00:26:03.560
- That's nice.

00:26:03.560 --> 00:26:05.456
- Shut the fuck up.

00:26:05.456 --> 00:26:06.824
- That did help out. It was nice.

00:26:06.824 --> 00:26:07.805
I was like, "Oh man,
these people are gonna

00:26:07.805 --> 00:26:09.930
see Graham lose."

00:26:09.930 --> 00:26:11.448
(all laughing)

00:26:11.448 --> 00:26:13.511
Yeah, it was amazing. It was really cool.

00:26:13.511 --> 00:26:16.806
But it did like kind of
shut out everything else.

00:26:16.806 --> 00:26:18.391
You're supposed to listen to your coach.

00:26:18.391 --> 00:26:19.889
Like, they're supposed to be calling shit.

00:26:19.889 --> 00:26:21.334
And it's like,

00:26:21.334 --> 00:26:23.258
he could have been speaking
different languages.

00:26:23.258 --> 00:26:24.888
He could be speaking in tongues.

00:26:24.888 --> 00:26:25.959
- Like while you're fighting?

00:26:25.959 --> 00:26:26.850
- Yeah, you're supposed to like.

00:26:26.850 --> 00:26:27.769
- How the fuck could you hear that?

00:26:27.769 --> 00:26:29.100
- Normally in boxing
you're supposed to like,

00:26:29.100 --> 00:26:30.164
your coach is supposed to be like,

00:26:30.164 --> 00:26:32.306
"Hey, fuckin' take it downstairs,
jab, get back on the jab."

00:26:32.306 --> 00:26:34.177
And like, I'm listening to none of that.

00:26:34.177 --> 00:26:36.021
(all laughing)

00:26:36.021 --> 00:26:37.361
- Is that like an amateur thing?

00:26:37.361 --> 00:26:40.159
Or is that like you just, when
you're like, for every boxer?

00:26:40.159 --> 00:26:43.147
- I think at every level
you're able to do that

00:26:43.147 --> 00:26:44.360
and I think it's a pro level.

00:26:44.360 --> 00:26:45.569
'Cause then they get to,

00:26:45.569 --> 00:26:47.612
they actually get to see from the outside.

00:26:47.612 --> 00:26:48.466
They'll be like, "Okay,

00:26:48.466 --> 00:26:49.678
it will work if you go downstairs

00:26:49.678 --> 00:26:51.049
and hit the body or whatever."

00:26:51.049 --> 00:26:52.282
- Right.
- Yeah.

00:26:52.282 --> 00:26:54.576
And so I listened to him a
little between the rounds.

00:26:54.576 --> 00:26:55.907
- A little bit.

00:26:55.907 --> 00:26:58.533
- Yeah, a little bit.
- You want some water? Yeah.

00:26:58.533 --> 00:27:00.156
- Sure. Yeah, yeah.

00:27:00.156 --> 00:27:01.573
It was super fun.

00:27:02.484 --> 00:27:04.181
My coach was training like

00:27:04.181 --> 00:27:05.649
three of the people who were fighting.

00:27:05.649 --> 00:27:08.559
So he was busy as hell that night.

00:27:08.559 --> 00:27:11.195
And it was really official backstage.

00:27:11.195 --> 00:27:13.596
Backstage was nerve-wracking.

00:27:13.596 --> 00:27:15.469
'Cause we get there and there's like

00:27:15.469 --> 00:27:17.478
the blue locker room
and the red locker room.

00:27:17.478 --> 00:27:18.873
And so we're split up by like,

00:27:18.873 --> 00:27:19.980
the people that we're fighting.

00:27:19.980 --> 00:27:22.961
And not a lot of people
know, but before the fight,

00:27:22.961 --> 00:27:26.424
there was a pro fight in that
same arena, just not streamed.

00:27:26.424 --> 00:27:29.045
And the pro, so there
was one pro in our room

00:27:29.045 --> 00:27:30.304
and one pro in their room,

00:27:30.304 --> 00:27:33.898
and our pro got TKOd first
round of his fight and he,

00:27:33.898 --> 00:27:35.554
so he came back to locker
room and he was like,

00:27:35.554 --> 00:27:37.718
"Fuck! Shit! Fuck!"

00:27:37.718 --> 00:27:39.160
And everyone's just.

00:27:39.160 --> 00:27:40.274
(all laughing)

00:27:40.274 --> 00:27:41.946
Just like.
- This giant dude.

00:27:41.946 --> 00:27:45.385
- Yeah, he's a huge
professional boxer, and I swear,

00:27:45.385 --> 00:27:46.959
and so we're like all
like nervous as hell.

00:27:46.959 --> 00:27:47.792
- Oh my God.

00:27:47.792 --> 00:27:49.614
- Yeah. Really bad vibes in our locker.

00:27:49.614 --> 00:27:51.485
The other locker room was like, cheering.

00:27:51.485 --> 00:27:54.762
I heard after they were
like, "Yeah, let's go!"

00:27:54.762 --> 00:27:55.979
And then he goes out to
the fucking "Minecraft,"

00:27:55.979 --> 00:27:57.934
like, "Turn that shit off!"

00:27:57.934 --> 00:28:00.712
(all laughing)

00:28:00.712 --> 00:28:03.815
- Yeah, and then we had Matt in our room.

00:28:03.815 --> 00:28:05.887
We saw him get just annihilated.

00:28:05.887 --> 00:28:07.054
- Did you have a TV?

00:28:07.054 --> 00:28:08.350
- We did, we had a TV.

00:28:08.350 --> 00:28:11.197
We didn't get to see anything
live until after our fight.

00:28:11.197 --> 00:28:13.637
So we're like in there watching the TV

00:28:13.637 --> 00:28:15.437
and we watched the first
round, like jaws hanging open,

00:28:15.437 --> 00:28:16.605
like, "What the fuck?

00:28:16.605 --> 00:28:19.371
Is that how all of them are gonna be?"

00:28:19.371 --> 00:28:20.431
We didn't know.

00:28:20.431 --> 00:28:22.493
We were like, "Is this what's happening?"

00:28:22.493 --> 00:28:24.535
- "What have we got ourselves into?

00:28:24.535 --> 00:28:26.265
I'm gonna do that? That's
gonna happen to me?"

00:28:26.265 --> 00:28:27.243
- I was so nervous.

00:28:27.243 --> 00:28:29.771
I was just like sitting
there, not talking to anyone.

00:28:29.771 --> 00:28:31.197
Will got some really good
footage of me just like

00:28:31.197 --> 00:28:32.778
sitting there with
headphones in just like,

00:28:32.778 --> 00:28:34.076
listening to music as much as I could.

00:28:34.076 --> 00:28:36.822
- So like, how does
like it compare to like

00:28:36.822 --> 00:28:38.035
when you went sparring?

00:28:38.035 --> 00:28:38.868
'Cause like it,

00:28:38.868 --> 00:28:41.223
was it something where kind
of like your experience just

00:28:41.223 --> 00:28:43.969
took over, you know, with
all the sparring experience?

00:28:43.969 --> 00:28:45.975
- I had to like try and be
kind of conscious about it.

00:28:45.975 --> 00:28:47.884
I had to consciously think like,

00:28:47.884 --> 00:28:49.089
"I will be making these moves,"

00:28:49.089 --> 00:28:51.918
but like sparring, it was crazy too.

00:28:51.918 --> 00:28:53.480
'Cause in sparring I did like,

00:28:53.480 --> 00:28:55.739
like five, six, seven sparring sessions

00:28:55.739 --> 00:28:57.020
with different people.

00:28:57.020 --> 00:28:59.689
I never won like a
single round of sparring.

00:28:59.689 --> 00:29:00.634
And you're not supposed to, you know,

00:29:00.634 --> 00:29:02.059
you're not winning in sparring, you know,

00:29:02.059 --> 00:29:03.017
it's not counted, but.

00:29:03.017 --> 00:29:03.850
- Who were you sparring against?

00:29:03.850 --> 00:29:05.183
- If my head fucking hurts after,

00:29:05.183 --> 00:29:06.246
I lost that round, you know?

00:29:06.246 --> 00:29:07.740
- Right.
- Yeah.

00:29:07.740 --> 00:29:09.934
- So I sparred against my coach first,

00:29:09.934 --> 00:29:11.943
and he's like, you know, a professional.

00:29:11.943 --> 00:29:13.283
And so he has to like, hold back.

00:29:13.283 --> 00:29:14.999
So you're not fighting someone really,

00:29:14.999 --> 00:29:16.784
you're fighting a good
guy who's holding back.

00:29:16.784 --> 00:29:17.993
It's like when you like
hold back in "Smash"

00:29:17.993 --> 00:29:19.534
against like, your girlfriend.

00:29:19.534 --> 00:29:22.405
(all laughing)

00:29:22.405 --> 00:29:25.655
- No reaction.
- She's right there too.

00:29:26.824 --> 00:29:29.048
- Yeah. And so I fought him.

00:29:29.048 --> 00:29:31.577
He shits on me constantly, obviously.

00:29:31.577 --> 00:29:33.609
We went to another, a gym.

00:29:33.609 --> 00:29:34.965
And they were very nice.

00:29:34.965 --> 00:29:37.204
We were trying to find
people for me to spar

00:29:37.204 --> 00:29:38.868
and there was this girl who's
like professional, she's,

00:29:38.868 --> 00:29:40.307
I was scared as fuck of her.

00:29:40.307 --> 00:29:41.845
I was like, "How long
have you been sparring?"

00:29:41.845 --> 00:29:43.810
She's like, "Since I was like nine."

00:29:43.810 --> 00:29:46.348
And I was like, "Okay,
that seems fine," and.

00:29:46.348 --> 00:29:47.607
- She kicked the shit outta you.

00:29:47.607 --> 00:29:49.622
- That was the hardest I've been punched.

00:29:49.622 --> 00:29:52.838
She hit me the hardest
out of anyone I sparred.

00:29:52.838 --> 00:29:53.925
She like.
- Oh, God.

00:29:53.925 --> 00:29:55.466
- It was cool to see different techniques,

00:29:55.466 --> 00:29:57.711
'cause my coach is very like,
fluid in all over the place.

00:29:57.711 --> 00:29:59.739
She had like incredible defense,

00:29:59.739 --> 00:30:00.828
she'd like block everything

00:30:00.828 --> 00:30:02.168
and frustrate the shit outta you.

00:30:02.168 --> 00:30:03.509
And then you'd come in and she'd like,

00:30:03.509 --> 00:30:04.482
had this really good check hook

00:30:04.482 --> 00:30:06.050
and she'd just blast your head.

00:30:06.050 --> 00:30:07.993
And like, getting hooked like that.

00:30:07.993 --> 00:30:10.513
That was, I felt the
dizziness on that day.

00:30:10.513 --> 00:30:12.107
- So how many times a
week are you sparring?

00:30:12.107 --> 00:30:13.223
Is it every single time you train?

00:30:13.223 --> 00:30:15.365
- Well, no, in the
beginning you need to like

00:30:15.365 --> 00:30:17.127
get up to snuff and then.

00:30:17.127 --> 00:30:18.541
- Need the basics.

00:30:18.541 --> 00:30:21.294
- And then when like my
coach thought I was ready,

00:30:21.294 --> 00:30:23.044
once or twice a week.

00:30:23.958 --> 00:30:25.479
- That's gotta be scary
though. Once or twice a week?

00:30:25.479 --> 00:30:26.597
- Yeah.

00:30:26.597 --> 00:30:28.156
- Getting your ass beat.

00:30:28.156 --> 00:30:29.426
- Yeah, yeah.

00:30:29.426 --> 00:30:31.087
And the second one is like contingent on

00:30:31.087 --> 00:30:32.918
how much you hurt from the first one.

00:30:32.918 --> 00:30:33.954
- Oh my, oof.

00:30:33.954 --> 00:30:35.460
- Yeah, so I got beat up by her.

00:30:35.460 --> 00:30:38.234
I got beat up by a 14-year-old child.

00:30:38.234 --> 00:30:40.246
- I believe that. I saw
some of the kids, though.

00:30:40.246 --> 00:30:41.854
- He was really good. I'm not
even embarrassed about that.

00:30:41.854 --> 00:30:43.910
He was really good.

00:30:43.910 --> 00:30:46.553
He's like a national champion for his age.

00:30:46.553 --> 00:30:48.466
He's like the best
14-year-old in the nation.

00:30:48.466 --> 00:30:49.926
- Of course he's gonna be better than you.

00:30:49.926 --> 00:30:51.169
- He was really great.

00:30:51.169 --> 00:30:52.608
He was like Aang from "Avatar"

00:30:52.608 --> 00:30:55.309
where he was like
floating around the ring.

00:30:55.309 --> 00:30:58.368
He was like moving just so
much and like, ba ba ba ba!

00:30:58.368 --> 00:30:59.348
And then get out.

00:30:59.348 --> 00:31:00.226
And then he was like, I can't hit him.

00:31:00.226 --> 00:31:01.926
And he's, ba ba ba ba! It was fucked.

00:31:01.926 --> 00:31:03.709
- You know, I've seen him like every anime

00:31:03.709 --> 00:31:05.549
where there's like a tournament,
like in "Hunter x Hunter".

00:31:05.549 --> 00:31:07.040
And you see the kid come on,

00:31:07.040 --> 00:31:09.532
you realize that you're
the fucking side character.

00:31:09.532 --> 00:31:11.155
(all laughing)

00:31:11.155 --> 00:31:14.072
- And then he teleports behind you.

00:31:16.451 --> 00:31:19.073
- Have you ever watched "Hajime no Ippo"?

00:31:19.073 --> 00:31:20.729
- I got clips from after the boxing,

00:31:20.729 --> 00:31:22.030
people were talking about it.

00:31:22.030 --> 00:31:24.073
- 'Cause I think you did
like one of the, I guess,

00:31:24.073 --> 00:31:25.909
moves similar to what they do.

00:31:25.909 --> 00:31:29.036
- Oh, the Dempsey roll?
- Dempsey roll!

00:31:29.036 --> 00:31:30.003
- You kinda did a Dempsey roll.

00:31:30.003 --> 00:31:31.922
- You know, Dempsey was a real guy.

00:31:31.922 --> 00:31:32.755
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:31:32.755 --> 00:31:34.545
- A real boxer. That's crazy.

00:31:34.545 --> 00:31:36.048
- He just took the move
and kind of made it like

00:31:36.048 --> 00:31:37.860
a more popular thing in the show, right?

00:31:37.860 --> 00:31:39.648
So normies know it, but
like everyone knew it,

00:31:39.648 --> 00:31:40.481
like, yeah, it was real.

00:31:40.481 --> 00:31:41.314
He's like one of the best, right?

00:31:41.314 --> 00:31:42.522
- He was very good, yeah.

00:31:42.522 --> 00:31:45.860
He had like a Mike Tyson style
thing where he just like,

00:31:45.860 --> 00:31:47.590
and then blocks.

00:31:47.590 --> 00:31:49.020
- I mean, that's what
like the main character.

00:31:49.020 --> 00:31:51.704
- You can't know the
anime without knowing it.

00:31:51.704 --> 00:31:53.503
- The power of golden anime.

00:31:53.503 --> 00:31:56.252
- It's like a very good defense.

00:31:56.252 --> 00:31:58.906
You're supposed to roll against a hook.

00:31:58.906 --> 00:32:00.881
That's when you're
supposed to do the roll.

00:32:00.881 --> 00:32:05.881
Yeah, but most of that shit
goes out the window. (laughing)

00:32:06.081 --> 00:32:08.072
- I tried a boxing class
like a few days ago.

00:32:08.072 --> 00:32:09.770
- Oh, I saw that. That was my coach.

00:32:09.770 --> 00:32:10.653
- Oh, him?

00:32:10.653 --> 00:32:11.609
Yeah. He was crazy.

00:32:11.609 --> 00:32:13.181
He was so fast.
- Michael, right?

00:32:13.181 --> 00:32:14.020
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:32:14.020 --> 00:32:15.127
- When he was doing like, he's like,

00:32:15.127 --> 00:32:16.055
"No, no, you gotta do it like this."

00:32:16.055 --> 00:32:18.686
I'm like, "What did you just
do?" I couldn't even see what.

00:32:18.686 --> 00:32:19.945
- He's so smooth.

00:32:19.945 --> 00:32:21.546
- I'm like, okay, okay.

00:32:21.546 --> 00:32:22.379
All right, okay.

00:32:22.379 --> 00:32:23.835
- He's like one of those anime characters

00:32:23.835 --> 00:32:24.693
where he punches once,

00:32:24.693 --> 00:32:26.893
and he's like, "I actually
punched three times."

00:32:26.893 --> 00:32:28.118
(all laughing)

00:32:28.118 --> 00:32:30.890
- But like four days afterwards,
my entire body hurts.

00:32:30.890 --> 00:32:32.695
- And dude, like you can't
use your phone, your hands,

00:32:32.695 --> 00:32:34.373
like your fingies are fucked.

00:32:34.373 --> 00:32:35.937
- My calves were like rubber.

00:32:35.937 --> 00:32:37.661
It was like, I couldn't walk.

00:32:37.661 --> 00:32:40.017
I felt like I looked like
an idiot when I was walking.

00:32:40.017 --> 00:32:40.850
- [Garnt] It's a full-time commitment.

00:32:40.850 --> 00:32:42.900
- But luckily I'm in America,
so walking is optional.

00:32:42.900 --> 00:32:44.677
(all laughing)

00:32:44.677 --> 00:32:46.161
But yeah, it was, dude.

00:32:46.161 --> 00:32:47.948
It was just like every
workout was a sprint.

00:32:47.948 --> 00:32:49.630
Like, I thought I was pretty fit,

00:32:49.630 --> 00:32:51.173
'cause I did a lot of running,

00:32:51.173 --> 00:32:53.213
but running did not prepare me for this.

00:32:53.213 --> 00:32:55.609
- Yeah. It's like you have
to do sprint training.

00:32:55.609 --> 00:32:57.420
- Just like a full on cardio workout.

00:32:57.420 --> 00:32:58.723
- It's full of like basically sprinting,

00:32:58.723 --> 00:32:59.841
every exercise.

00:32:59.841 --> 00:33:01.531
- Yeah, no, it really is.

00:33:01.531 --> 00:33:03.882
Like when you're like doing the treadmill

00:33:03.882 --> 00:33:05.313
and you're supposed to like run in sprints

00:33:05.313 --> 00:33:06.340
instead of just constantly.

00:33:06.340 --> 00:33:07.490
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:33:07.490 --> 00:33:10.175
- 'Cause it's like, you're
trying to imitate the rounds.

00:33:10.175 --> 00:33:11.481
Yeah, yeah.

00:33:11.481 --> 00:33:12.555
- It was fucked up. It was fucked up.

00:33:12.555 --> 00:33:14.679
- That looked like a cool
class, though. It looked sweet.

00:33:14.679 --> 00:33:15.893
- Yeah. It was kind of cool.

00:33:15.893 --> 00:33:17.416
I mean, I think it was like, pretty big.

00:33:17.416 --> 00:33:18.432
So it was hard to really feel like

00:33:18.432 --> 00:33:21.050
you were learning anything
like, tailored to you.

00:33:21.050 --> 00:33:22.024
But I mean, it's good though.

00:33:22.024 --> 00:33:23.690
It was like.
- You only had one class.

00:33:23.690 --> 00:33:25.470
So you know, there's more room to grow.

00:33:25.470 --> 00:33:27.279
- Could you do that five days
a week for months at a time?

00:33:27.279 --> 00:33:28.552
- No, if, okay.

00:33:28.552 --> 00:33:30.022
I think I would, like,
what I was saying is like,

00:33:30.022 --> 00:33:31.305
I think I would enjoy
it more if I was like,

00:33:31.305 --> 00:33:33.246
just me and him, and
then I could take my time

00:33:33.246 --> 00:33:35.151
and then I could, he
could really give me like,

00:33:35.151 --> 00:33:36.149
"All right, you're struggling here."

00:33:36.149 --> 00:33:37.651
'Cause he would just be like, "All right,

00:33:37.651 --> 00:33:39.594
12 of you do jabs," and
then he would maybe like,

00:33:39.594 --> 00:33:40.638
"Yeah, it's okay."

